Unsupervised methods have also been used, for example using a Bayesian
approach in the one-shot learning of object categories [1], but their error rate has
not been encouraging.
The previous works' results have typically been obtained with relatively large
training sets, with the prediction accuracy considerably decreasing when limited
training data is available [14]. However, the primary goal of few-shot learning is
not classification, but to verify the closeness of an unknown input to a reference.
This problem is computationally simpler, and its main challenge is the projection
of the input and reference to an appropriate embedding space for comparison.
In this work, we present a simplified Siamese neural network with less
computational complexity and low parameter count, which should enable it to
learn from fewer examples and make an embedded system implementation easier.
